# device-layer-0002.
# The torch, the flashlight beside the camera: through AVCaptureDevice on iOS (and a Mac, which has none),
# CameraManager on Android, and a camera track's `torch` constraint in a browser.
#
#   torch-state       on, off, or unavailable (no torch on this device)
#   set-torch(state)  state is on or off. Answers the torch's state after, or unavailable, or denied when the
#                     platform needs the camera grant first
#
# A host with no such capability (the server, the memory host) answers `unavailable`. Every answer is text from the
# closed set above, so an app compares strings and no platform enum ever reaches it.

load ./native/{platform}/torch
  find read-torch
  find write-torch

task torch-state
  like text
  send back
    call read-torch

task set-torch
  take state, like text
  like text
  send back
    call write-torch
      read state
